.TH FREEWAVE 1 2026-08-31 freewave "User Commands"
.SH NAME
freewave \- album\-focused music client for MPD and Subsonic
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B freewave
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B freewave
presents a music library as a grid of album covers and keeps the play
queue central to the interface.
It connects either to a Music Player Daemon server
.RB ( mpd (1))
or to a Subsonic\-compatible server such as Navidrome, Gonic, Ampache
or LMS.
.PP
Servers are configured from within the application; there are no
command\-line options for choosing or connecting to one.
Credentials are stored in the desktop keyring when one is available.
.PP
Features include drag\-and\-drop queue management, server\-native
playlists and favorites, a real\-time audio visualizer, and MPRIS
desktop integration.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version, the compiled\-in backends and the enabled features,
then exit.
This is resolved before the GUI is initialised, so it does not require a
display.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SPDLOG_LEVEL
Logging verbosity, one of
.BR trace ", " debug ", " info ", " warn ", " error ", " critical
or
.BR off .
Defaults to
.BR debug .
.TP
.B QT_LOGGING_RULES
Standard Qt logging category rules.
Applied after freewave's own defaults, so it can re\-enable categories
the application silences.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/xeyes.org/freewave.conf
Settings, including configured server profiles.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mpd (1),
.BR mpc (1)
